WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:03.380
One heatwave never causes just one problem.

00:03.430 --> 00:05.850
It sets off a chain.

00:06.500 --> 00:08.510
This is the Common Shade map.

00:08.560 --> 00:10.840
Extreme heat sits in the centre.

00:10.890 --> 00:15.240
Around it, ten systems, from water and food to health and work.

00:15.290 --> 00:20.430
Each dot is a harm, 90 in all, each with its sources.

00:21.080 --> 00:24.090
Tap a dot, such as power cuts.

00:24.140 --> 00:25.970
The map lights up what feeds it,

00:26.020 --> 00:28.400
and what it sets in motion.

00:29.050 --> 00:33.620
Each harm opens a card: what happens, the evidence behind it,

00:33.670 --> 00:36.270
and the cycles it is caught in.

00:36.920 --> 00:41.230
Some links curve back on themselves. These are vicious cycles.

00:41.280 --> 00:43.110
Cooling demand heats the city,

00:43.160 --> 00:46.360
and a hotter city needs even more cooling.

00:47.010 --> 00:50.940
The green marks are levers: actions that can cut a link.

00:50.990 --> 00:57.190
Each one shows who can act, how soon it works, and where it has been tried.

00:57.840 --> 01:03.260
Switch on a package of actions, and see which of the 21 cycles it could help interrupt.

01:03.310 --> 01:09.870
It is a guide for thinking, not a forecast: real effects depend on reach and quality.

01:10.520 --> 01:12.240
Start with the harm you see.

01:12.290 --> 01:13.700
Follow the lines.

01:13.750 --> 01:15.620
Find the lever within reach.

01:15.670 --> 01:19.370
Explore the map at beattheheat.asia.
